      "writtenOn": "2024-11-05T09:55:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems like wallpapering over a problem, not fixing it.\n\nHave we tried other approaches? For example, looks like we could call AppOpsManager#checkPackage and see if it returns an error or throws. Or we could call PackageManager#getPackagesForUid and checked if the passed-in package name is in the list.\n\nAlso, as Patrick says, won\u0027t this CL change the behaviour in production of calling isTetheringSupported on from a non-system user? That doesn\u0027t seem like something we can safely do.\n\nAlso, what\u0027s the point of try/catching here? AFAICT we know that this code:\n- Will never throw if the passed-in user is the same as the current user.\n- Will always throw if the passed-in user is not the same as the current user.\n\nIf we can\u0027t fix this problem, then at least we should do something that\u0027s easier to understand, such as:\n\n    // TODO: figure out how to get the uid for a package in another user.\n    // - PackageManager#createContextAsUser will throw IAE because networkstack only\n    //   runs in the system user and not necessarily in the passed-in user.\n    // - PackageManager#getPackageUidAsUser requires INTERACT_ACROSS_USERS_FULL\n    //   which networkstack does not have.\n    if (!UserHandle.getUserHandleForUid(Process.myUid()).equals(user)) {\n        return -1;\n    }\n\nand leave the rest of the code as is.\n\nIf we do need to try/catch, then can we at least catch the right type of Exception here instead of blanket-catching everything? Even if you don\u0027t change this, please add a comment to explain why we need to catch an ecxception here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 213,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "8fdb60d58a4a4f525fb622da223c0cde55f7f149",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
