      "writtenOn": "2024-11-06T23:13:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If #1 works, why limit the usage to networkstack only? Why not use it everyhere?\n\nYes, #1 works. Would it be possible that this change get made in a separate CL so that if something were it break it wouldn\u0027t need to revert the tethering stack of CLs again. Created b/377758490 to track this effort, and added this to the comments.\n\n```\nCan we add a CTS test that ensures it works? It seems quite easy:\n\nRegister a callback\nAttempt to start tethering with the invalid package\nCheck that the callback is called back with a permission error.\n```\n\nThere is already some existing CTS test that\u0027s verifying that correct call is passing:\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Connectivity/tests/cts/tethering/src/android/tethering/cts/TetheringManagerTest.java;l\u003d401?q\u003d%22.registerTetheringEventCallback(%22\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main\n\nThe invalid package testing would be kind of complicated. In my understanding, CTS test calling through TetheringManager will alway result in a valid packageName. To inject an invalid packageName the CTS test would need to access TetheringService directly from a binder call. This doesn\u0027t seem like a case that we would normally test through CTS. If you know a better way to fake a packageName, please let me know",
      "parentUuid": "977443d0_bcef7aa0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 213,
        "endChar": 26
